!20 - Source Library/Equipment Manuals/Positioners/instruction-manual-fisher-fieldvue-dvc7k-h-digital-valve-controller-en.pdf

# Historic Educational Services archive — browse-only, unverified, ~140 files
# in deeply-nested folders (some exceed the Windows path limit). The catalogue
# note "Historic Educational Services Training Content.md" one level up stays
# tracked; the archive contents themselves do not need versioning.
20 - Source Library/Legacy & Archive/Historic Educational Services Training Content/

# Legacy Educational Services course deck — 3.4GB, was completely unprotected
# (no existing .pptx pattern matched this path). Kept in the vault and
# browsable, same as the Historic archive above, just never tracked.
20 - Source Library/Legacy & Archive/Legacy Educational Services Courses/17101 Control Valve Instrumentation - Basic v Jan 2026.pptx

# ── Render-check Node deps (regenerable: npm --prefix "40 - Engine/render" install) ──
40 - Engine/render/node_modules/
40 - Engine/render/baseline.txt

# ── Narration pipeline (Chatterbox voice cloning, all local) ────────
# venv and generated audio are regenerable; the reference voice clip is
# personal audio and deliberately NOT versioned. Scripts, glossary, and
# voice-config.json (the chosen settings) ARE tracked.
narration/.venv/
narration/output/
voice/

# ── Stray artifact ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# invalid 20-byte file at the vault root from an aborted regen; the real
# course data is 10 - Courses/.../Presentation/course/course-data.js
/course-data.js

# Python bytecode and one-off render scratch files. Both regenerate; the
# venv rule above already covers narration/.venv.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
40 - Engine/render/_tmp-*.mjs

# One-off experiment, dry-run and preview OUTPUT under 10 - Courses.
# Pipeline-generated and reproducible from it -- mostly rendered PNGs,
# ~18 MB when this rule was added (2026-10-09).
#
# Named by family, deliberately NOT a blanket "_*" rule. Several
# underscore-prefixed directories ARE tracked and are real: _Template
# Gallery/, _generator/, _Origination Test - */, _Template Proof - ch3/,
# and a _preview/ under 14101. core.ignorecase is true here, so a loose
# pattern would also catch that last one by case alone. A blanket rule
# would quietly stop showing new files added to any of them.
#
# Note this reverses earlier practice: the vault has committed this kind
# of artifact before (the _Origination Test and _Template Proof trees).
# Going forward these stay out of history.
10 - Courses/_Domain-Tier Dry Run*/
10 - Courses/_Preview*/
10 - Courses/*/Presentation/build/_*-prototype/
